# WorldForge architecture (hard)

## Boundaries

- Geography algorithms live only in `crates/worldforge-core`.
- Host adapters (`worldforge-photocraft`, CLI) stay thin.
- Do not import Chess Studio, Tauri, React, Medusa, or chess rules into this repo.
- Chess Studio may consume WorldForge **exports later**; WorldForge never owns campaigns.

## PhotoCraft adapter

- Target: `wasm32-unknown-unknown` with **zero imports**.
- ABI exports: `pc_abi_version`, `pc_manifest`, `pc_alloc`, `pc_filter`, plus `memory`.
- Render by global document coordinates; bands must stitch seamlessly.
- Prefer instruction-cheap per-pixel paths; keep coast glow / neighborhood work gated.
- Any plugin-cost-affecting edit must run instruction-budget checks before completion.
- Do not mark plugin work done unless host/plugin tests show no instruction-budget overrun at default settings.

## Determinism

- Separate `Seed::stream` names per generation stage.
- Bump `GENERATOR_VERSION` when seed meaning changes.
- Same inputs ⇒ same `f32` samples.

See root `AGENTS.md` for commands and forbidden list.
